librsswitch
===========
librsswitch (remote socket switch) is a Raspberry Pi Linux library for
controlling remote controlled power sockets. The library emulates the encoder
chip within the power socket remote control, so a separate 433 MHz sender is
needed.

librsswitch is written in C and heavily inspired by rcswitch-pi [1], which is
based on rc-switch [2].


Supported devices
-----------------
At the moment librsswitch supports the following devices:

- REV 008345 (PT2260-R4S)
- Pollin 2605 (PT2262)


Hardware setup
--------------
See the librsswitch Wiki [3] for a detailed description of how to set up the
entire hardware.


Software setup (Raspberry Pi / Raspberry Pi 3)
-----------------------------------------------
GPIO access goes through libgpiod [4], not bcm2835 -- install the dev
package on the Pi:
 $ sudo apt install libgpiod-dev

Build with the matching Makefile target from examples/basic/ or
examples/network/:
 $ make rpi     # Raspberry Pi (32-bit ARM)
 $ make rpi3    # Raspberry Pi 3 (aarch64)
 $ make bbb     # BeagleBone Black (sysfs GPIO, no libgpiod needed)
 $ make x86_64  # host build, GPIO calls are stubbed out


Software setup (cross compiling on x86_64)
------------------------------------------
Install an ARM/aarch64 cross toolchain (e.g. via your distro's
gcc-arm-linux-gnueabihf / gcc-aarch64-linux-gnu packages), then build
with the matching target -- the Makefile sets CROSS_COMPILE for you
based on the target and picks up libgpiod headers from
/usr/include and /usr/local/include:
 $ make rpi     # arm-linux-gnueabihf-gcc
 $ make rpi3    # aarch64-linux-gnu-gcc

libgpiod itself (headers + library) needs to be available for the
target architecture in your cross sysroot -- either cross-build it
from source or install your distro's cross-dev variant if one exists.


Usage
-----
socket_send(uint dev, uint group, uint socket, uint data);

- dev: Vendor ID (check the table of supported devices)
- group: Socket group
- socket: Socket within a socket group
- data: 1 = On, 0 = Off

[1] https://github.com/r10r/rcswitch-pi
[2] http://code.google.com/p/rc-switch/
[3] https://github.com/graznik/librsswitch/wiki
[4] https://git.kernel.org/pub/scm/libs/libgpiod/libgpiod.git/
